#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:128
msgid "Redirect after payment (URL)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:132
msgid "Optional. When the payment confirms, send the buyer here (a custom thank-you, a digital-download page, etc.) instead of staying on the order-received page. {order_id} and {order_key} are substituted: {order_key} only for a URL on this same site, so the order token is never leaked to a third-party domain. Leave empty for the default WooCommerce behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:135
msgid "Refund link valid for (days)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:138
msgid "When you refund a Monero order, the buyer gets a claim-link to enter a receive address (a Monero payment never reveals the sender). This is how long that link stays valid. After it expires the buyer sees a clear message to contact you, and you can reissue the link from the order screen with one click. Set 0 to never expire."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:142
msgid "How payments are verified"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:146
msgid "Auto-detect in WordPress: no server (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:147
msgid "Buyer taps “I’ve paid”: no server"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:148
msgid "Auto-detect via your xmr-pay agent (advanced)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:150
msgid "All three are non-custodial (funds go straight to your address). <strong>Auto-detect in WordPress</strong> needs no backend: WordPress scans the chain itself (with your view key, against a public node) and completes the order: no buyer action, nothing to run 24/7. <strong>Buyer taps “I’ve paid”</strong> is the lightest: the buyer submits the transaction ID and WordPress verifies it (no scanning). <strong>Agent</strong> uses the separate xmr-pay daemon you run. The “No-server settings” below (address, view key, nodes) apply to the two no-server options; the “Agent settings” apply only to Agent mode."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:153
msgid "No-server settings (Auto-detect & “I’ve paid”)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:155
msgid "Used by both no-server modes: “Auto-detect in WordPress” and “Buyer taps I’ve paid”. Your private view key stays on your own server (we never hold a spend key: funds go straight to your address). WordPress fetches transactions from a public node and verifies them itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:158
msgid "Network"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:162 includes/class-xmrpay-setup.php:253
msgid "Your Monero address"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:165
msgid "<strong>The network is set by this address</strong>: a 4… address is mainnet, 5…/7… is stagenet. To go from stagenet to mainnet (or back), change this address plus the view key and node to that network’s. Buyers pay here; each order gets a unique amount so payments can’t be confused."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:168 includes/class-xmrpay-setup.php:257
msgid "Private view key"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:170
msgid "Your wallet’s PRIVATE VIEW key (not the spend key). View-only: it can see incoming payments but cannot spend. <strong>More private:</strong> instead of storing it here, put <code>define('XMRPAY_VIEW_KEY', '…');</code> in wp-config.php: then it stays out of the database, this screen, and backups. A value here is used only if the constant is not set."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:173
msgid "Monero node(s)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:176
msgid "Add public or private Monero nodes in priority order. Authentication is configured separately for each node. Block lookup fails over to the next node. Settlement requires every configured node to answer and agree on the transaction and its block height; an unavailable or disagreeing node pauses payment confirmation. Keep them on the same network and well synced. The node never sees your view key."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:179 includes/class-xmrpay-setup.php:276
msgid "Confirmations required"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:182
msgid "0 = accept as soon as it’s seen (fast, mempool); 1 = first block (~2 min); 10 = fully unlocked (safest for high value)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:186
msgid "Underpayment tolerance (XMR)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:189
msgid "Accept a payment that falls short by up to this much (dust/rounding). 0 = exact. It can never reach the price, so a near-zero payment never settles an order."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:192
#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:516
msgid "Check setup"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:196
msgid "Agent settings (advanced)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:198
msgid "Used only when the “Agent” mode is selected. The separate xmr-pay daemon you run (see docs/AGENT.md) holds your view key and does the scanning: this plugin only talks HTTP to it. Detection policy (confirmations, tolerance, expiry) is set ON the agent (XMR_MIN_CONFIRMATIONS, XMR_TOLERANCE_XMR, XMR_EXPIRY_HOURS). Leave blank if you use a no-server mode."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:201 includes/class-xmrpay-setup.php:288
msgid "Agent URL"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:204
msgid "Base URL of your scanner-agent. Must point to localhost (127.0.0.1, ::1, or localhost)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:207 includes/class-xmrpay-setup.php:292
msgid "Agent token"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:209
msgid "The AGENT_TOKEN configured on the agent. Required in Agent mode, including for localhost connections."
msgstr ""

