#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:225 includes/class-xmrpay-setup.php:222
msgid "Pricing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:227
msgid "How the cart total becomes an XMR amount. Tip: set your store currency to <strong>XMR</strong> to price natively in Monero: then no price feed is used."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:230
msgid "Price source"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:234
msgid "CoinGecko (live fiat → XMR)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:235
msgid "Your own price source (a URL)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:236
msgid "Fixed rate (set it yourself)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:238
msgid "How a fiat total converts to XMR (ignored when the store currency is already XMR). For CoinGecko or a custom source, set a <strong>Fixed rate</strong> too and it’s used automatically as a fallback if the live feed is ever unavailable. Checkout requires an available live rate or a valid fixed rate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:241
msgid "CoinGecko API key"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:243
msgid "Optional: your own CoinGecko Demo/Pro key, so the price feed is yours and not rate-limited. Leave empty to use the free public endpoint."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:246
msgid "Custom price URL"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:249
msgid "Used with “Your own price source”. A URL returning JSON. <code>{currency}</code>/<code>{CURRENCY}</code> are substituted with the store currency code. It should return the price of 1 XMR in your store currency."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:252
msgid "Rate JSON path"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:255
msgid "Dot-path to the number in the JSON response, e.g. <code>monero.usd</code> or <code>data.rates.XMR</code>. Leave blank if the response body is the bare number."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:258
msgid "Fixed rate / fallback"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:261
msgid "The price of 1 XMR in your store currency. Used as the rate with “Fixed rate”, and as the automatic fallback for the live sources if their feed is down."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:264
#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:584
msgid "Confirmations"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:267
msgid "Shown to the buyer; the agent enforces its own XMR_MIN_CONFIRMATIONS. Raise both for high-value carts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:270
msgid "Test amount (XMR)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:273
msgid "TEST ONLY: charges this exact XMR amount, ignoring the cart total. It is honoured ONLY when your agent is on stagenet/testnet (run \"Test connection\" first); on mainnet it is ignored, so it can never fix the price on a live store. Leave empty in production."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:276
msgid "Auto-cancel after (hours)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wc-gateway-xmrpay.php:279
msgid "Cancel an unpaid order this many hours after it was placed (frees reserved stock). 0 = never. Payments after cancellation require manual reconciliation. WordPress scanning may not detect a transfer that is still awaiting mining when the order expires. Leave this at 0 to keep waiting. This window doubles as your rate-drift guard: if you price in fiat, an order paid much later settles at the XMR amount locked at checkout, so set this to how long you are willing to honour that rate (e.g. 12–24). If you price natively in XMR, the amount owed never changes: leave it at 0."
msgstr ""

